# Implementation Plan - Film Institution Registration Hub

Create a minimalist, light-themed student registration hub for a Film Institution using Node.js, Express, and vanilla HTML/CSS/JS.

## Proposed Changes

### Backend Setup

#### [NEW] [package.json](file:///c:/Users/ELANGO%20N%20D/OneDrive/Desktop/SUMMER/FIlm%20Institute%20Registration/package.json)
Initialize a Node.js project containing standard metadata and dependencies:
- `express` for the HTTP server.
- `nodemon` as a development dependency for automatic server restarts (optional, but convenient).
- `start` script executing `node server.js`.

#### [NEW] [server.js](file:///c:/Users/ELANGO%20N%20D/OneDrive/Desktop/SUMMER/FIlm%20Institute%20Registration/server.js)
Setup Node/Express backend:
- Run on Port `3000`.
- Use `express.json()` middleware to parse JSON payloads.
- Serve static files from the `public/` directory using `express.static('public')`.
- Implement `POST /api/register` to:
  - Check validation (Full Name, Email, Phone, and Course).
  - Return `400 Bad Request` if any validation fails.
  - Append valid registrations to `students.json`.
  - Log successful submissions to the console.
  - Return success status.

### Frontend Setup

#### [NEW] [public/index.html](file:///c:/Users/ELANGO%20N%20D/OneDrive/Desktop/SUMMER/FIlm%20Institute%20Registration/public/index.html)
A split-screen viewport layout using Google Font `Plus Jakarta Sans`:
- **Left Column**: Course catalog containing 3 cards:
  - "Direction & Screenwriting"
  - "Cinematography"
  - "Post-Production & Editing"
  - Each card will have a subtle gradient placeholder representing the aesthetic visual style.
- **Right Column**: A fixed form section:
  - Inputs: Full Name (`text`), Email (`email`), Phone (`tel`), Selected Program (`select` dropdown).
  - Status container for success/error messages.
- Links to `style.css` and `script.js`.

#### [NEW] [public/style.css](file:///c:/Users/ELANGO%20N%20D/OneDrive/Desktop/SUMMER/FIlm%20Institute%20Registration/public/style.css)
Elegant, bright UI using modern CSS practices:
- Set up CSS custom variables for consistent spacing, colors (`#eeeeef` thin borders, soft gradients, slate text colors).
- Use `Plus Jakarta Sans` as the primary typography.
- Split-screen layout using CSS Grid or Flexbox (`1vh` viewport heights).
- Implement interactive scale transitions (`transform: scale(1.02)`) on course card hovers.
- Add active card highlighting with a distinctive thin border and subtle shadow when a course card is selected.
- Create input field focus states with smooth transitions.

#### [NEW] [public/script.js](file:///c:/Users/ELANGO%20N%20D/OneDrive/Desktop/SUMMER/FIlm%20Institute%20Registration/public/script.js)
Interactions and network calls:
- Attach event listeners to course cards to add a `.selected` class and synchronize the dropdown selection.
- Intercept registration form submit action.
- Fetch API call to `/api/register` with JSON body payload.
- Handle responses and update the DOM status container with appropriate feedback/error styling.

